terms.definition:
Blaze Bedding uses a bed explosion to clear blocks around a Nether Fortress Blaze spawner, increasing the valid dark space where Blazes can spawn. The runner detonates the bed from cover, then quickly extinguishes fires because bright blocks can suppress spawning.

{{media:0}}

It can save mining time, but a poor setup can damage the runner or block spawn positions.

Blind travel is a Java 1.16 RSG strategy in which a runner moves through the Nether to a selected coordinate and builds an exit portal without first using an Eye of Ender to learn the stronghold's direction or distance. The goal is to emerge near a first-ring Stronghold, after which an eye can correct the route.

{{media:0}}

It is distinct from educated and calculated travel.

Bridge Bastion is one of the four Bastion Remnant layouts. It is distinguished by its large ruined bridge and a prominent gold-block structure often called the gold chalice.

{{media:0}}

Speedrun routes use its exposed gold and layout-specific piglin positions, so it is routed differently from Housing, Stables, and Treasure bastions.

A Bucket Portal is a Nether portal built by casting a lava pool into obsidian with a water bucket instead of mining ten obsidian blocks. Runners place water and redirect lava source blocks into a portal frame, then light it with flint and steel or a flintless setup.

{{media:0}}

Fast construction makes accessible lava pools one of the most valuable early RSG resources.

Calculated Travel is a Nether-travel method that estimates both the direction and distance to a stronghold from precise Eye of Ender measurements, usually with a calculator. The runner converts the estimated Overworld target to Nether coordinates and builds a second portal nearby.

{{media:0}}

It can produce a much closer exit than a blind or direction-only travel.

Divine Travel is a Java Edition 1.16.1 technique that uses the position of a Nether fossil in a particular chunk to infer where a stronghold can be reached through another portal. It depends on world-generation correlations and is highly version-specific.

{{media:0}}

It does not work in MCSR Ranked, where the Overworld and Nether seeds are generated independently.

Educated Travel is a two-portal Nether-travel method that uses an Eye of Ender throw after the first exit to learn the stronghold's direction. The runner re-enters the Nether, moves along the corresponding direction, and builds a second exit portal nearer the stronghold ring.

{{media:0}}

It improves direction over a blind travel without calculating a precise stronghold position.

Fortress Navigation is the skill of reading Nether Fortress structure pieces to reach a Blaze spawner quickly. Runners distinguish the exterior bridge section, where spawner platforms generate, from the interior section and use junctions, balconies, staircases, and the lava-well room to avoid searching dead ends.

{{media:0}}

Good navigation turns an unfamiliar layout into a small set of informed route choices.

Housing Bastion is one of the four Bastion Remnant layouts. It contains two ramparts connected through a central housing section, with layout-specific gold, chests, and piglin positions.

{{media:0}}

Runners identify it quickly because its safe and efficient route differs from Bridge, Stables, and Treasure bastions.

Mapless is a Java Edition technique for locating Buried Treasure without obtaining its map. The runner first uses a version-specific Pie Chart profiler path and chunk-boundary changes to identify the treasure chunk, then digs at chunk-relative X/Z coordinates `9, 9`.

{{media:0}}

That coordinate only locates the chest inside a known treasure chunk; using `9, 9` in an arbitrary chunk does not find treasure.

Microlensing is a Java 1.16 debug-screen technique that samples entity counts while the runner narrows and turns the camera to infer the direction of a hidden Bastion. A concentrated change in the entity reading can reveal where the structure's piglins are behind terrain.

{{media:0}}

The method improves search decisions but does not reveal an exact route, and it depends on version-specific F3 behavior.

A Nether Fortress is a Nether structure whose Blaze spawners provide the Blaze Rods required for Eyes of Ender. In Java 1.16.1 routes, runners often visit a Bastion first for pearls, obsidian, and Fire Resistance, then locate and navigate a fortress for rods.

{{media:0}}

Fortress layout and spawner access strongly affect a run's pace.

Nether Travel uses the Nether's 1:8 horizontal coordinate scale to cover Overworld distance quickly.

{{media:0}}

In Java Edition RSG, a runner can build another portal in the Nether so its Overworld exit is closer to a stronghold. Blind, Educated Travel, and Calculated Travel differ in how precisely the runner estimates that destination.

A one cycle defeats the Ender Dragon during a single perch at the exit portal. In modern Java speedruns, runners normally time bed explosions against the dragon's head as it perches; respawn-anchor variants or backups also exist.

{{media:0}}

The technique depends on the post-1.9 dragon fight and does not describe older pre-1.9 End fights.

A Perch is the Ender Dragon's landing sequence at the central exit portal. Runners prepare beds around the portal and wait for a favorable perch because it creates the main window for a One Cycle.

{{media:0}}

Perch behavior is partly random and can be standardized by formats such as MCSR Ranked.

Stables Bastion is one of the four Bastion Remnant layouts. Its hoglin-stable sections, multiple ramparts, and distributed loot create routing and safety problems distinct from the other layouts.

{{media:0}}

Speedrun routes account for its variable structure pieces, hoglins, gold access, and piglin collection.

A Stronghold is an underground Overworld structure containing the Portal Room required to reach the End. Eyes of Ender lead toward the nearest Stronghold's starting area rather than directly to the portal, and the frame activates only when all twelve slots contain eyes.

{{media:0}}

Finding the correct area, locating the Starter Staircase, and navigating the generated branches are separate speedrun skills.

Treasure Bastion is one of the four Bastion Remnant layouts. It has a large central treasure room with lava, gold blocks, and a magma cube spawner.

{{media:0}}

That vertical, hazardous layout requires its own route for collecting gold and bartering without losing time or dying.

Triangulation estimates a stronghold location by comparing Eye of Ender directions from two or more measured positions. The intersection of those direction lines gives a target estimate.

{{media:0}}

The diagram shows the geometry; in practice, stronghold calculators can account for measurement error, but accurate throws and inputs still matter.

{{media:1}}

The tutorial demonstrates how those measured throws become a usable target during a run.

A zero cycle is an advanced End-fight technique that intercepts and kills the Ender Dragon during its initial flight, before a normal perch cycle. Established setups use a specific End spike, orientation, height, and timed bed or respawn-anchor explosions.

{{media:0}}

Exact setups depend on the Minecraft version and on whether the run is vanilla RSG or MCSR Ranked.
